  "title": "Laura L NDE 6241",
  "date": "10-31-1996",
  "content": "After delivering twins prematurely, I had retained placenta and was losing too much blood. I was afraid of blood transfusions and wouldn't give consent. I continued to bleed for three days. On the third day of losing blood, I felt a detachment with my loved ones. I was afraid. Then, feelings went away. The next thing I remember, I was on the ceiling of the hospital room looking at my body and the doctors and nurses. I wasn't afraid or aware that was my body lying there! I wondered why they all were so concerned over that person. A second later, I was in this wonderful light! It was all around me and felt tremendous. Overwhelming, it felt so good that I have no words to describe its wonderfulness!!!! Then, in another second, I was standing on a river made of liquid light! There was grass and landscape but it was all made of this light or had the light in it. It is hard to describe. As I said earlier, it was so AWESOME! I couldn't believe how wonderful this river was and I turned to look upstream and didn't get to see. I was back in the hospital bed receiving blood. I was SO angry! I would rather have stayed in the place made of light! I forgot a lot of things I used to know. I learned many things again but have never recovered some memories of my life. It took a few years to get over the anger, but no longer fear death at all! I used to be afraid of death. I came back a different person. It changed me in many ways.",
